# DP03 code layout

Before reading or changing anything under `cpp/`, read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. It maps every
file to the pass it belongs to, the beams (b1, b2, b4, b_V, b_G, P beams), and the reference
section or equation.

- `cpp/main.cpp` is a unity build: it `#include`s the parts in a fixed order. Most parts are
  fragments of `class DP03` or of `main()`, not standalone headers. Do not reorder the
  includes or compile a part on its own.
- Keep each file under about 1,500 lines, with a short header saying what it computes in
  paper notation. Put new code in the folder of its pass (`pass1/`, `pass2/`, `pass3/`),
  `exact/`, `diag/`, `energy/`, `common/` or `cli/`.
- Build with `make` (paper-v1 flags; never `-ffast-math` or FMA contraction). After any
  change to `cpp/`, run `make check` (V and G identity) and compare logZ against the tag
  `paper-v1` on the paper preset before claiming values are unchanged.
- When files move or a pass changes, update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` in the same commit.
